                <pb facs="0474" n="409" sameAs="frus:frus1936v03/pg409"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.01/65: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Liberia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Walton</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Monrovia</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-12-15T09:00:00-00:44">December 15, 1936—9
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 11:20 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>44. Confidentially and reliably informed Great Britain will recognize Liberia
                    Wednesday, December 16th, at 11 a.m., when British colleague presents
                    credentials.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Walton</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
